{"id": "EUVD-2026-103758", "enisaUuid": "bf29c167-55cc-3814-be9c-6d09a4de5255", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/nouveau/dmem: pin VRAM for the whole registered range\n\nCommit c32287471077 (\"gpu/drm/nouveau: enable THP support for GPU memory\nmigration\") grew the device-private region that\nnouveau_dmem_chunk_alloc() registers from DMEM_CHUNK_SIZE to\nDMEM_CHUNK_SIZE * NR_CHUNKS, but left the VRAM buffer object backing that\nregion at DMEM_CHUNK_SIZE.\n\nnouveau_dmem_page_addr() returns chunk->bo->offset plus the page's offset\nwithin the registered region, so every page past the first chunk resolves\nto VRAM outside the buffer object.\n\nSize the buffer object to the region it backs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/06c69c64686a31783c8bec6495dc22822d38c4ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64ca4cdd1031206424e6455f0ae4fb0560d8f46a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-84w9-cx8r-cxrf", "CVE-2026-98518"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4f35a9b0-1886-36db-a03a-33f79ebfcc1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "7212f3ee-2cda-3192-8523-724dee023762", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "7e31c19f-7f3f-3374-865a-c6a6dbbe8b6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9e7d8f79-babe-32d0-b97d-9bb083c7d045", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c3228747107705d47c7e9a03598a434a0380cb73 <06c69c64686a31783c8bec6495dc22822d38c4ce"}, {"id": "a08b5b7d-137e-38d8-92ae-cc91a324a9e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "dcaa2212-494c-3fd8-af35-54f783b28750", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c3228747107705d47c7e9a03598a434a0380cb73 <64ca4cdd1031206424e6455f0ae4fb0560d8f46a"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2e2a667b-c47d-3ae0-bbc3-f93acc5bcb96", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}